volume.text:
Task-relevant continuity can be maintained through selective, noncanonical and role-separated realization rather than one globally maximal or representationally identical carrier, provided every current realization remains sufficient for a named obligation, preserves stable relation/role semantics, and carries an explicit regime-and-trajectory warrant. Adaptation, rerouting or reallocation must not be mislabeled as expansion: a true growth claim requires a separate boundary-crossing witness under perturbations that stress neighboring non-invariants, and crossing or materially shifting that boundary requires revalidation of carrier sufficiency, role semantics and relational continuity before the new state inherits prior warrant.


Rank-necessity / removal witness:
- remove 1H.ujF6: the closure loses selective/path-sensitive actualization, moving-frontier pressure and evidence-responsive reallocation;
- remove 1H.9gYl: it loses explicit semantic role separation, exact-obligation sufficiency and composite-assurance discipline;
- remove 1H.uSiP: it loses the distinction between improved access/rearrangement and genuine expansion of reachable support;
- remove 1H.hs7W: it loses the warrant for coherent function across noncanonical heterogeneous carriers and pressure-aligned invariance testing.
All four are therefore necessary for the complete volume.

Task-relevant capability can be maintained without keeping one globally maximal or canonical active representation when predictable/reacquirable structure remains cheap, flexible residual support is actualized and reallocated only where current context or pressure makes it necessary, and the warrant for that realized state travels with both the operating envelope and the inference/adaptation trajectory. Efficiency and continuity are earned only while local actualization remains compatible with the source/task relation and frontier-sensitive probes show that the operating regime still holds; when the frontier moves, representation and allocation must be revalidated rather than replayed as though nothing changed.


Rank-necessity / removal witness:
- remove S.sgMu: the closure loses the explicit stable-structure/residual-economy distinction and the obligation-scoped efficiency/evidence envelope;
- remove S.uIc5: it loses inference-time context-selective actualization under otherwise unchanged parameters;
- remove S.fF61: it loses longitudinal frontier migration and the requirement to revalidate warrant through update history;
- remove S.cugW: it loses materially grounded local support creation, bounded persistence, and evidence-responsive capacity reallocation.
All four are therefore necessary for the complete volume.
